# mdfly-server environment. Copy to .env and fill in real values.
#
# One file for both paths: deploy/compose.yaml reads it as `env_file: ../.env`
# on the app, postgres, and migrate services, and a local `go run` picks it up
# with `set -a; . ./.env; set +a`. .env is gitignored — never put a real secret
# in this example.
#
# Values below are the production shape. For local dev, uncomment the block at
# the bottom: a repeated key wins, so nothing above needs deleting.
#
# Production walkthrough: docs/deploy/oracle-vm-setup.md

# --- Postgres (read by the postgres container itself) -------------------------
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD and the password inside DATABASE_URL must match.
POSTGRES_DB=mdfly
POSTGRES_USER=mdfly
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME_LONG_RANDOM

# --- Required -----------------------------------------------------------------
# `postgres` and `redis` are compose service names, resolved by Docker's embedded
# DNS. sslmode=disable is correct: the hop never leaves the bridge network. The
# Redis password must match requirepass in deploy/redis.conf.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://mdfly:CHANGE_ME_LONG_RANDOM@postgres:5432/mdfly?sslmode=disable
REDIS_URL=redis://:CHANGE_ME_LONG_RANDOM@redis:6379
BASE_URL=https://mdfly.dev

R2_ENDPOINT=https://<account-id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
R2_BUCKET=mdfly
CDN_BASE_URL=https://cdn.mdfly.dev

# --- CDN purge (ADR-0012) -----------------------------------------------------
# Either one empty leaves the purge-drain job unregistered: writes still enqueue
# durably, nothing contacts the edge.
CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID=
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=

# --- Optional, defaults shown -------------------------------------------------
ADDR=:8080
LOG_LEVEL=info
SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT=15s
PURGE_DRAIN_INTERVAL=15m
LIFECYCLE_GC_INTERVAL=1h
ABANDON_GRACE=1h
BLOB_DELETE_GRACE=24h

# --- Local dev overrides ------------------------------------------------------
# `make dev-seed` starts Postgres on localhost:5432 with these credentials. An
# empty REDIS_URL boots the rate limiter off and empty CLOUDFLARE_* leaves the
# purge drain unregistered — both are supported modes.
#
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://mdfly:secret@localhost:5432/mdfly?sslmode=disable
# REDIS_URL=
# BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080
# R2_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:9000
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=minioadmin
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=minioadmin
# CDN_BASE_URL=http://localhost:9000/mdfly
